-- title:
--   Fixed field of the level automorphisms for q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((X))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (itself the $\mathbb Q$-subfield of $\mathbb Q((X))$ generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,d\,j$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M'$), is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the analogous base change of the $q$-expansion field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ and group `levelH q M'` $=\ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times)$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field and $\xi\in k_0$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Put $H_1=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'\cap\ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times)$, let $K$ be the $k_0$-subfield of $k_0((X))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, let $G\le \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ be generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lies in $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and satisfies `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, i.e. for all weights $k$, all weight-$k$ forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\ne 0$ over $\mathbb Q$, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficient embedding of $p_f/p_g$, and all ring maps $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$; and let $K_0=K^G$. Then, for the $k_0$-algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` coming from $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in `fieldBar q M'` whose elements are exactly those whose Laurent coefficients all lie in $k_0$, there is a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\sim}F_0$ such that the coefficientwise image along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the Laurent series of each $f\in K_0$ is the Laurent series of $\varphi(f)$, and such that whenever $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` has its coefficient embedding in $K$ and in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends it to the image of $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by the containment hypothesis.
--
--   This is the comparison, in the case $q=2$ and with the auxiliary level $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ rigidifying the moduli problem, between the fixed field of the automorphisms of the level-$q^2M'$ $q$-expansion field attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and the subfield of the geometric level-$q$ function field cut out by $k_0$-rationality of all Laurent coefficients, the isomorphism being the identity on $q$-expansions and on rational level-$M'$ modular functions. It feeds the diamond-operator descent statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_linkedScalars_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_algEquiv_fixedField_levelField_coeffMap_eq_linkedScalars_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
